  "worked_solution": "First, we find the limit of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 2}f(t) & =⟨{lim}_{t\\to 2}\\,(6-{t}^{3}),\\,{lim}_{t\\to 2}\\,({t}^{2}-6),\\,{lim}_{t\\to 2}\\frac{16}{{t}^{3}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6-{2}^{3},{2}^{2}-6,\\frac{16}{{2}^{3}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,-2,2⟩ \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 2}g(t) & =⟨{lim}_{t\\to 2}\\,(5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3-t)),\\,{lim}_{t\\to 2}\\,\\sqrt{6-t},\\,{lim}_{t\\to 2}\\,2t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3-2),\\sqrt{6-2},2(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,2,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use properties of limits to calculate the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 2}[f(t)\\times g(t)] & ={lim}_{t\\to 2}f(t)\\times {lim}_{t\\to 2}g(t) \\\\  & =⟨-2,-2,2⟩\\times ⟨5,2,4⟩ \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot 4-2\\cdot 2)\\,i-((-2)\\cdot 4-5\\cdot 2)\\,j+((-2)\\cdot 2-5\\cdot (-2))\\,k \\\\  & =-12\\,i+18\\,j+6\\,k \\\\  & =⟨-12,18,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$",
